      "extract": "\\label{sec1} The low-lying eigenvalues of the QCD Dirac operator are of great importance for the understanding of the spontaneous breaking of chiral symmetry in QCD. In Euclidean space, the Dirac operator reads $i\\slash D=i\\slash\\partial+g(\\lambda^a/2)\\slash A^a$, where $g$ is the coupling constant, $\\lambda^a$ are the generators of SU($N$)-color, and $A_\\mu^a$ are the gauge fields. The corresponding eigenvalue",
      "extractCut": true
