      "extract": "\\label{sec22} The polynomials $p_n^{(N_f)}(x,M)$ can be constructed by applying a standard formula~\\cite{Bate51} in the theory of orthogonal polynomials. In our case, it reads \\begin{equation} p_n^{(N_f)}(x,M) \\ = \\ \\frac{1}{Z_n^{(N_f)}(M)} \\int d[X] \\Delta_n^2(X) \\prod_{i=1}^n w^{(N_f)} (x_i,M) (x-x_i) \\ . \\label{poly} \\end{equation} This is an integral over $n$ variables $x_i$ ($i=1,\\ldots,n$). We notice that $n$",
