        }
      ],
      "extract": "\\label{sec32} In lattice simulations, the performance of an algorithm is frequently determined by the magnitude of the smallest eigenvalue. It is therefore of interest to compute an analytical result for the distribution of the smallest eigenvalue, $P^{(N_f)}(\\lambda_{\\rm min},m)$, in the framework of RMT. This is the subject of this section. The RMT result should be universal and identical with that of full QCD",
